.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt APROPOS 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm apropos ,
.Nm whatis
.Nd search the manual page index
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm apropos
.Op Fl afkt
.Op Fl C Ar file
.Op Fl M Ar path
.Op Fl m Ar path
.Op Fl O Ar outkey
.Op Fl S Ar arch
.Op Fl s Ar section
.Ar expression ...
.Nm whatis
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl C Ar file
.Op Fl M Ar path
.Op Fl m Ar path
.Op Fl S Ar arch
.Op Fl s Ar section
.Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility searches the index of each manual directory, the file
.Pa oxdoc.db
that
.Xr makewhatis 8
builds, and lists the pages matching
.Ar expression :
their names, section and one-line description.
The
.Nm whatis
utility lists the pages with a
.Ar name
among their names.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Show the matching pages in full, through
.Xr man 1 ,
instead of listing them.
.It Fl C Ar file
Read the manual directories from
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa /etc/man.conf .
.It Fl f
Search as
.Nm whatis
does: each argument is a whole word to find in the pages' names, ignoring
case.
.It Fl k
Search as
.Nm apropos
does, the default.
.It Fl M Ar path
Search the indexes of the colon-separated manual directories in
.Ar path
instead of the default ones.
.It Fl m Ar path
Search the directories in
.Ar path
before the others.
.It Fl O Ar outkey
Show the values of the key
.Ar outkey
for each page instead of its description, sorted and separated by
.Ql # .
.It Fl S Ar arch
Only list pages for the architecture
.Ar arch ,
or for any.
.It Fl s Ar section
Only list pages of
.Ar section .
.It Fl t
Search the full text: each word in
.Ar expression
is the term
.Cm Tx= Ns Ar word .
.El
.Ss Expressions
An expression is made of terms, joined by
.Fl a
.Pq and
and
.Fl o
.Pq or .
Two terms without an operator between them are joined by
.Fl o ,
and
.Fl a
binds more tightly.
Parentheses, as separate arguments, group terms.
.Pp
A term has the form
.Oo Ar key Ns Oo , Ns Ar key ... Oc Ns Po Cm = | Cm ~ Pc Oc Ns Ar value .
With
.Cm = ,
it is true of a page with a value of one of the
.Ar key Ns s
containing
.Ar value ,
ignoring case; with
.Cm ~ ,
of a page with a value matching the extended regular expression
.Ar value
.Pq see Xr re_format 7 ,
with case, unless
.Fl i
comes before the term.
Without a
.Ar key ,
a term searches the names and the description.
A term without
.Cm =
or
.Cm ~
searches the names and the description with
.Ar value
as a regular expression, ignoring case.
.Ss Keys
The keys are the
.Xr mdoc 7
macros whose values
.Xr makewhatis 8
records, and a few others:
.Bl -column "St, At, Bx, Fx" "description" -offset indent
.It Cm \&Nm Ta the page's names
.It Cm \&Nd Ta its one-line description
.It Cm sec Ta its section
.It Cm arch Ta its architecture
.It Cm \&Sh , \&Ss Ta its section and subsection titles, except the standard ones
.It Cm \&Xr Ta its cross references, as Ar name Ns Pq Ar section
.It Cm \&Fl , \&Cm , \&Ar , \&Ic Ta flags, modifiers, arguments and commands
.It Cm \&Ev , \&Pa , \&Er Ta environment variables, paths and error numbers
.It Cm \&In , \&Lb Ta header files and libraries
.It Cm \&Fn , \&Fa , \&Ft Ta function names, arguments and types
.It Cm \&Va , \&Vt , \&Dv Ta variables, types and constants
.It Cm \&An , \&Lk , \&Mt Ta authors, links and mail addresses
.It Cm \&Cd , \&Ms , \&Tn Ta configuration, symbols and trade names
.It Cm \&Em , \&Sy , \&Li Ta emphasized, bold and literal text
.It Cm \&St , \&At , \&Bx , \&Fx , \&Nx , \&Ox , \&Dx , \&Bsx Ta standards and systems
.It Cm \&Tx Ta every word of the page's text, in lower case
.It Cm any Ta all of the above but Cm \&Tx
.El
.Pp
Pages written in
.Xr man 7
only have names, a description and full text.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MANPATH
.It Ev MANPATH
The manual directories, as for
.Xr man 1 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/man.conf -compact
.It Pa oxdoc.db
the index in each manual directory
.It Pa /etc/man.conf
the manual directories
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 if it found a page, and 1 if it found none or the
arguments were wrong.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Pages mentioning file systems in their names or descriptions:
.Dl $ apropos 'file ?system'
.Pp
Pages in section 3 using both
.Va optind
and
.Va optarg :
.Dl $ apropos -s 3 Va=optind -a Va=optarg
.Pp
Pages referring to
.Xr getty 8 ,
with those references:
.Dl $ apropos -O \&Xr \&Xr=getty
.Pp
Pages whose text mentions a password:
.Dl $ apropos -t password
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr man 1 ,
.Xr man.conf 5 ,
.Xr makewhatis 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
and
.Nm whatis
utilities first appeared in
.Bx 2 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD; its expressions and keys follow
.Xr mandoc 1 Ns 's
.Nm .
.Sh BUGS
The names of a page are listed in the order its NAME section gives them,
which is not always the order of other systems.
